  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 2d1e83780892b5c4592add1c4998da52, type: 3}
  m_Name: NatureFacts
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::FactPack
  category: 4
  facts:
  - Trees can communicate through underground fungal networks.
  - Some jellyfish are biologically immortal.
  - Ants never sleep.
  - A group of owls is called a parliament.
  - Otters hold hands when they sleep.
  - Cows have best friends.
  - Bamboo is the fastest growing plant.
  - Sharks have been around longer than trees.
  - Seahorses are monogamous and mate for life.
  - Hummingbirds are the only birds that can fly backwards.
  - A snail can sleep for three years.
  - Koalas have unique fingerprints like humans.
  - Tigers have striped skin, not just striped fur.
